France plans to make its development aid to seven African countries conditional on greater cooperation in the fight against illegal immigration to the French island territory of Mayotte, as the issue becomes increasingly politicised ahead of the French presidential election next year.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/98391ee4-a15a-11f1-ac0e-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6866ZR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/98391ee4-a15a-11f1-ac0e-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6866ZR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">aa5d8488-a200-11f1-b7e4-dd9f6f304afc</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 11:30:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/98391ee4-a15a-11f1-ac0e-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6866ZR.jpg">© Marine Gachet/AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Science and Technology</category><title>Climate change is ‘very visible from space’, France's Sophie Adenot tells RFI</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/science-and-technology/20260827-climate-change-is-very-visible-from-space-france-s-sophie-adenot-tells-rfi</link><description>
In an exclusive interview with RFI and sister TV channel France 24 from the International Space Station, French astronaut Sophie Adenot described the signs of climate change she can see from orbit and how she overcame major technical problems during her second spacewalk earlier this week.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e33f3ff8-a16a-11f1-ba2e-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Depuis-l-ISS-Sophie-Adenot-a-r%C3%A9pondu-aux-questions-de-Baptiste-Coulon-et-Sylvain-Rousseau-pour-RFI-et-France24-ie-26-ao%C3%BBt-2026-3.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e33f3ff8-a16a-11f1-ba2e-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Depuis-l-ISS-Sophie-Adenot-a-r%C3%A9pondu-aux-questions-de-Baptiste-Coulon-et-Sylvain-Rousseau-pour-RFI-et-France24-ie-26-ao%C3%BBt-2026-3.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bebd94ac-a1f3-11f1-b19c-89dd84255de2</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 12:09:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e33f3ff8-a16a-11f1-ba2e-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Depuis-l-ISS-Sophie-Adenot-a-r%C3%A9pondu-aux-questions-de-Baptiste-Coulon-et-Sylvain-Rousseau-pour-RFI-et-France24-ie-26-ao%C3%BBt-2026-3.png">© RFI</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Looking up: French sailors ditch GPS to rediscover celestial art of navigation</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260827-looking-up-french-sailors-ditch-gps-to-rediscover-celestial-art-of-navigation</link><description>
Astronaut Sophie Adenot made history this month as the first French woman to perform a spacewalk. Back on Earth, space enthusiasts across France are finding their own ways to reach for the stars. In the fourth of a five-part series, RFI meets amateur sailors learning to navigate by the stars, using a technique that allows them to find their position without GPS or onboard electronics.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4247340c-a151-11f1-9f33-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Margo-l-un-des-quatre-stagiaires-%C3%A0-bord-du-Whirlwind-s-exerce-%C3%A0-la-manipulation-du-sextant.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4247340c-a151-11f1-9f33-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Margo-l-un-des-quatre-stagiaires-%C3%A0-bord-du-Whirlwind-s-exerce-%C3%A0-la-manipulation-du-sextant.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4d36764e-a1f5-11f1-b80f-89dd84255de2</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 14:03:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4247340c-a151-11f1-9f33-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Margo-l-un-des-quatre-stagiaires-%C3%A0-bord-du-Whirlwind-s-exerce-%C3%A0-la-manipulation-du-sextant.jpg">© Baptiste Coulon / RFI</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Second person dies after man deliberately drives into crowd in Caen</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260827-second-person-dies-after-man-deliberately-drives-into-crowd-in-caen</link><description>
