Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu arrives in the French overseas territory of Mayotte on Wednesday to try to speed up the reconstruction of the archipelago, 18 months after Cyclone Chido caused widespread destruction.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/adc78510-5d78-11f0-9d19-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-64FJ6ZQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/adc78510-5d78-11f0-9d19-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-64FJ6ZQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9efd8954-a12d-11f1-9d4b-c95053c4254a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 10:46:09 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/adc78510-5d78-11f0-9d19-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-64FJ6ZQ.jpg">© PATRICK MEINHARDT / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>How Dolly Parton became much more than country music’s 'backwoods Barbie'</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260825-how-dolly-parton-became-much-more-than-country-music-s-backwoods-barbie</link><description>
Back in 2008 at age 62, Dolly Parton released a single proclaiming she was "just a backwoods Barbie, too much makeup, too much hair."
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/57f47062-a0b1-11f1-bfdf-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/b1eafd7dce9336939880e6ee32dd960e7e66b898.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/57f47062-a0b1-11f1-bfdf-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/b1eafd7dce9336939880e6ee32dd960e7e66b898.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">58e35876-a0b1-11f1-9051-87f52546a6be</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 18:18:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/57f47062-a0b1-11f1-bfdf-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/b1eafd7dce9336939880e6ee32dd960e7e66b898.jpg">© Robyn Beck / AFP/File</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Nigerian president orders rescue operation after mass kidnapping in mosque</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260826-nigerian-president-tinubu-orders-rescue-operation-after-mass-kidnapping-in-mosque</link><description>
Nigerian President Bola Tinubu has ordered the military and other security agencies to launch an immediate rescue operation after the mass kidnapping of worshippers during an attack on a mosque in the north-central Niger State last week.
